course: dictionary
lesson: 15733
title: Translocate: moving life to safer homes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Translocate is a formal word, often used in science. It means to move something from one place to another, especially wild animals or plants, to a new home where they are safer. Look at the word parts: trans means across, and locate means to place. Put them together and you get the idea of moving something across to a new place.
explain: «The rangers translocated six rhinos to a national park.» The rangers did not just take the rhinos for a walk. They moved them to a new home to keep them safe. So translocated means moved to a new place, and the words «to a national park» show where they went.
explain: Scientists also use translocate for plants. «Sugar is translocated from the leaves through the stem.» Here it does not mean moving a thing about. It means carrying food, such as sugar, through the plant from one part to another.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The rangers moved six rhinos to a national park.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Move is the everyday word; translocate is the careful science word.
fact: Translocate means to move something from one place to another, especially wild animals or plants, to a safer home.
fact: «Translocated» is the past tense of translocate, as in «The rangers translocated the rhinos.»
fact: In plant science, to translocate means to carry sugar through the stem from the leaves to other parts of the plant.
fact: «Phloem» is the name for the tubes in a plant that carry sugar: «Sugar is translocated through the phloem.»
fact: In everyday talk, people say move or relocate instead of translocate.
exercise: «The rangers translocated six rhinos to a national park.» What does translocated mean? | *Moved to a new place, to keep them safe | Painted with bright colours | Fed and then sent home the same day | Counted carefully
exercise: In a plant, what does it mean to translocate sugar? | *To carry it through the stem from the leaves to other parts | To wash it off the leaves | To burn it in the sun
exercise: Which everyday word could replace translocate? | Ignore | Freeze | Shout | *Relocate
test: «Beavers were translocated to a quiet river, where they could build dams.» Which word could replace translocated without changing the meaning much? | *Moved | Counted | Hidden | Chased
test: Why would rangers translocate animals? | To make them lose their way | *To keep them safe in a new home | To leave them where they are
exam: Which sentence uses translocate correctly? | The sky translocated into a bright blue colour. | *The scientists translocated the wild kiwis to an island where they would be safe. | The children translocated the whole class song loudly.
